onboarding-p1-title = Welcome to NeuroFeed
onboarding-p1-lead = Neurofeedback shows your brain activity back to you, second by second, so you can learn to steer it.
onboarding-p1-point1 = Pick a protocol (what to train), sit still, and follow the sound and the circle.
onboarding-p1-point2 = Sessions are short: 5–20 minutes. Regular practice matters more than length.
onboarding-p1-point3 = Not a medical device. It does not diagnose or treat anything.
onboarding-p2-title = Fit the headband
onboarding-p2-lead = Good contact is everything. The fit check waits until all pads read clean.
onboarding-p2-point1 = Forehead pads sit flat, just above the eyebrows; ear pads touch skin behind the ears.
onboarding-p2-point2 = Move hair aside and wipe the skin; a little water helps dry skin.
onboarding-p2-point3 = Relax your jaw and face: clenching and blinking show up as noise.
onboarding-p3-title = Calibration
onboarding-p3-lead = Each session starts by measuring your own baseline, so the threshold fits you today.
onboarding-p3-point1 = Follow the spoken instructions (eyes open or closed) for about a minute.
onboarding-p3-point2 = Dirty seconds (blinks, movement, bad pads) are left out of the baseline.
onboarding-p3-point3 = You can reuse the last baseline for the same device and protocol.
onboarding-p4-title = Training and trust
onboarding-p4-lead = During training you are rewarded when the feature is above your threshold percentile.
onboarding-p4-point1 = The trust pane shows what every second really was: in zone, below, held back or dirty.
onboarding-p4-point2 = Held-back seconds are not rewarded even if they look good: the signal was not trustworthy.
onboarding-p4-point3 = The threshold adapts slowly so you stay at about the reward rate you chose.
onboarding-p5-title = Your data stays here
onboarding-p5-lead = Recordings, notes and settings are stored only on this device.
onboarding-p5-point1 = Add a pseudonymous subject id in Settings → General if you want to tell sessions apart.
onboarding-p5-point2 = Export a session from History (.neurofeed or EDF) to share or analyse it.
onboarding-p5-point3 = AI agents can only control the app if you switch on the bridge in Settings → About.
